  "body": "The difference between the two RFCs is summarized in https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc8288#appendix-C, and a full diff is at http://tools.ietf.org/tools/rfcdiff/rfcdiff.pyht?url1=https://tools.ietf.org/rfc/rfc5988.txt&url2=https://tools.ietf.org/rfc/rfc8288.txt. \n\nThis is mostly editorial, although there are a couple changes in what Link headers are valid between the RFCs. Chromium [already follows the RFC8288 rule for parameters without values](https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/components/link_header_util/link_header_util.cc?l=178&rcl=caeb5244297852de45c2f8baa5a8101aeff89865), although I don't see a test for it, or any tests for the Link header in web-platform-tests. We seem to parse more loosely than either RFC requires.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5127/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Dec 4, 2019, 11:35 PM UTC (c23cb7c)\">/infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5127/836294c...c23cb7c/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Dec 4, 2019, 11:35 PM UTC (c23cb7c)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5127/references.html\" title=\"Last updated on Dec 4, 2019, 11:35 PM UTC (c23cb7c)\">/references.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5127/836294c...c23cb7c/references.html\" title=\"Last updated on Dec 4, 2019, 11:35 PM UTC (c23cb7c)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5127/semantics.html\" title=\"Last updated on Dec 4, 2019, 11:35 PM UTC (c23cb7c)\">/semantics.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5127/836294c...c23cb7c/s